  "agent": {
    "note": "**M2.4-fix² — the cursor is now baked m0 rects, not `geq`.** Your call: *solve it with rects, we have the whole graph.* Right on both counts.\n\n**Why 013 failed (and 012 before it):**\n\n| Attempt | Mechanism | Failure |\n|---|---|---|\n| 012 | `drawbox` on transparent base | alpha-dropped → invisible in render |\n| 013 | `drawbox replace=1` | `drawbox` evaluates x/y/w/h **once** → frozen upper-left |\n| (geq) | `geq` per-pixel alpha mask | animates, but constant-rgb + alpha-mask is fragile (solid-fills on any alpha loss) **and** `O(pixels × frames)` slow |\n\n**The fix — the cursor SNAPS, so model it as snaps.** It never interpolates between two positions; it jumps to each new bound as the parse advances. So it's now **one enable-gated inline-mask ring per step** — the exact machinery the dashed splits and the Frame outline already use. Only one is lit at a time (`between(t, start, next)`); consecutive identical positions collapse to keep the layer count down.\n\n**Verified in the actual ffmpeg render** (not just preview): the ring frames cell **1**, then jumps to cell **2** as the walk advances — it moves this time.\n\n**Wins beyond speed:** deterministic, no per-pixel alpha fragility (the exact bug that burned 012/013), Rect-Thesis-native. On perf: a 2s test showed parity (mask rasterization is the floor for both paths), but `geq`'s cost grows linearly with frames — on a 12s × 1920×1080 render it would dominate, whereas the rings rasterize once and just composite. One caveat: each ring is a sibling overlay layer, so very dense layouts press on the ~25 overlay-depth ceiling (tracked in the `.ai` overlay-depth candidate); the collapse + M5/M6 own that.",
    "question": "Does the orange cursor now **move** through the render — leading each cell as it emits (frame cell 1 → cell 2 → cell 3 → cell 4), reading as a clean thin outline? If yes, M2 cursor is settled and I'll start **M3 (DSL-string panel)**.",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "other",
        "label": "geometry-cursor"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "propose",
        "summary": "M2.4-fix² — cursor rebuilt as enable-gated inline-mask rings (baked rects, one per step) replacing the geq cursor; animates + robust + cheaper on long renders."
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "013"
      }
    }
  }
